    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0649" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg527"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Preston.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 18,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have your telegrams of the 16th and 18th instant requesting this Department to
                    order the detention of the <hi rendition="#italic">Carondelet</hi> at Newport
                    News and the <hi rendition="#italic">Conserva</hi> at New York. In accordance
                    with your previous requests <pb facs="0650" n="528" xml:id="pg528"/> full
                    opportunity has been given for application to the judicial and customs
                    authorities for investigation of facts in relation to both these vessels. The
                    nationality and ownership of the <hi rendition="#italic">Conserva</hi>, and the
                    destination and objects of the cargo of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Carondelet</hi>, have been properly made the subject of investigation and
                    decision by the officials of the appropriate Departments of this Government, and
                    nothing has been brought to my knowledge which gives me authority to overrule,
                    or ground to question their action in the premises.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
